# Build output paths and the size each may reach before the `builds` tool
# deletes it whole for the next build to refill (cargo mostly from sccache).
# scripts/build-layout.sh, run first by the hooks and every build script, links
# each path to /Volumes/Builds/bae/<checkout>/<path>, deletes the build copies
# in it that no build has used for three days (the tool's default), and then
# applies the caps. The hooks and build scripts run cargo through
# scripts/cargo.sh, which records each build copy cargo uses, rebuilt or up to
# date.
#
# Caps are about twice a fresh build of each: host 9.8G, macOS bridge 7.4G,
# Android 6.4G, iOS 12G; the macOS app's .build holds two DerivedData trees
# (check.sh's and run.sh's) of 2.2G each fresh and the Swift packages both
# resolve into, 3.0G; BaeKit's `swift build` 4.4G; BaeKit/Frameworks, the
# xcframeworks build-macos.sh and build-ios.sh make, 1.4G and 1.9G; the others,
# the Android bridge's debug info among them (0.4G per ABI), are under 1G.
# target is about three times its fresh build: main's reached 26G across a day
# of clippy, tests and coven bumps, and a delete there loses the person's warm
# host build.
#
# path                                cap
target                                30G
target-macos                          15G
target-ios                            24G
target-android                        13G
bae-macos/bae/.build                  20G
bae-ios/bae/.build                    10G
BaeKit/.build                         9G
BaeKit/Frameworks                     7G
bae-android/.gradle                   1G
bae-android/debug-symbols             2G
bae-android/app/build                 2G
bae-android/bridge/build              1G
bae-android/fastvalues/build          1G
bae-avalonia/obj                      1G
bae-avalonia/bin                      1G
bae-avalonia/bae-avalonia.Tests/obj   1G
bae-avalonia/bae-avalonia.Tests/bin   1G
